ns\\\\\\\\n   Lambda Add-Permission statement so API Gateway principal may invoke:\\\\\\\\n     aws lambda add-permission \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       --function-name ContactFormHandler \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       --statement-id apigw-contact-prod \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       --action \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda:InvokeFunction\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       --principal apigateway.amazonaws.com \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n       --source-arn \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:execute-api:{region}:{acct}:{api-id}/*/POST/contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nNo additional IAM role required because REST integration uses Lambda ARN + explicit permission above.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. Implementation Checklist (Deterministic Steps)\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n1. (SES) Verify sender identity + obtain production access.\\\\\\\\n2. (IAM) Create ContactFormLambdaRole and attach policies.\\\\\\\\n3. (Lambda) Zip/function code, create ContactFormHandler with env vars.\\\\\\\\n4. (API) Create ContactFormAPI, /contact resource, POST method (Lambda proxy), enable CORS.\\\\\\\\n5. Deploy to stage \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"prod\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and capture Invoke URL.\\\\\\\\n6. Test end-to-end: POST {name,email,message} JSON; expect 200 and email delivered.\\\\\\\\n7. Configure monitoring/alarms on Lambda error count & SES bounce/complaint metrics.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThis concludes the complete backend architecture plan for the contact form.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T01:01:10.378Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"My Attendants have delivered exceptional work. Gideon's plan for the content pipeline and Seratt's plan for the communications backend are both thorough, secure, and well-architected. They have covered all the required details, from resource configuration to IAM policies.\\n\\nMy task now