he root of the content bucket. This JSON file will contain metadata for all posts (title, path, date), allowing the frontend to easily generate a list of all news updates.\\\\n\\\\n4.  **IAM Role (`ContentProcessorLambdaRole`):**\\\\n    *   A dedicated IAM role will be created for the Lambda function.\\\\n    *   **Permissions:** The attached policy will grant the minimum necessary permissions: `s3:GetObject` on the uploads bucket, `s3:GetObject`/`s3:PutObject` on the content bucket, and standard permissions for writing logs to CloudWatch.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Part 2: Contact Form Backend Architecture\\\\n\\\\nThis system provides a secure and reliable backend for the website's contact form.\\\\n\\\\n1.  **API Endpoint (API Gateway):**\\\\n    *   A REST API will be created with a `/contact` resource that accepts `POST` requests.\\\\n    *   The endpoint will be configured with **Lambda Proxy Integration**, immediately forwarding requests to our backend function.\\\\n    *   **CORS** will be enabled to allow the frontend website to make requests to the API.\\\\n\\\\n2.  **Lambda Function (`ContactFormHandler`):**\\\\n    *   **Trigger:** Invoked by the API Gateway.\\\\n    *   **Action:** Parses the incoming JSON body (`name`, `email`, `message`), performs basic validation, and uses the AWS SDK to send an email via SES.\\\\n    *   **User Experience:** The `Reply-To` header of the email will be set to the user's provided email address, allowing the HOA to reply directly to the sender.\\\\n    *   **Configuration:** Key details like the 'To' and 'From' email addresses will be managed securely via Lambda environment variables.\\\\n\\\\n3.  **Email Service (AWS SES):**\\\\n    *   **Identity Verification:** An HOA email address (e.g., `contact@your-hoa.com`) will be verified in SES to act as the recipient and a `no-reply@your-hoa.com` address will be verified as the sender.\\\\n    *   **Production Access:** A request will be filed with AWS to move the account ou