\"}\\\\\\\\n              }\\\\\\\\n            },\\\\\\\\n            ReplyToAddresses=[email]  # So recipient can reply directly\\\\\\\\n        )\\\\\\\\n  4. On SES success (HTTP 200), return { statusCode: 200, body: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sent\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" }.\\\\\\\\n  5. Catch & log exceptions → return 500 with generic failure JSON.\\\\\\\\nSecurity:\\\\\\\\n  – Escape/strip CRLF to prevent header injection.\\\\\\\\n  – Use AWS X-Ray (optional) for tracing.\\\\\\\\n  – CloudWatch Logs and metric filters for error alarms.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. Amazon SES Configuration\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nRegion: Prefer us-east-1 or region with production-ready SES.\\\\\\\\nSteps:\\\\\\\\n  a. Verify an identity (email or domain) to serve as FROM address.\\\\\\\\n       # Example: aws ses verify-email-identity --email-address no-reply@example.com --region us-east-1\\\\\\\\n  b. For domain verification: add DNS TXT + optional DKIM CNAMEs per SES instructions.\\\\\\\\n  c. Await IdentityVerification token status = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Success\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\\n  d. (Sandbox lift) Open an SES production-sending request to move account out of sandbox OR keep contacts within verified TO addresses.\\\\\\\\n  e. Optionally create a Configuration Set for advanced deliverability analytics.\\\\\\\\n  f. OPTIONAL: Enable \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Easy DKIM\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and SPF (TXT) for improved inbox placement.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. IAM Roles & Policies\\\\\\\\n-------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. Lambda Execution Role: ContactFormLambdaRole\\\\\\\\n   Trust Policy:\\\\\\\\n     Service = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n   Attached Policies:\\\\\\\\n     1. AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole   (logs)\\\\\\\\n     2. Inline policy ContactFormSESSend:\\\\\\\\n        {\\\\\\\\n